[00:10.20]When will the writer see the play? | 作者什么时候能看上戏？
[00:15.14]'The play may begin at any moment,' I said. | “剧马上就要开演了，”我说。
[00:19.47]'It may have begun already,' Susan answered. | “也许早已开演了，”苏珊回答说。
[00:24.55]I hurried to the ticket office. | 我匆匆赶到售票处。
[00:27.78]'May I have two tickets please?' I asked. | “我可以买两张票吗？”我问。
[00:32.35]'I'm sorry, we've sold out,' the girl said. | “对不起，票已售完，”那位姑娘说。
[00:37.10]'What a pity!' Susan exclaimed. | “真可惜！”苏珊大声说。
[00:41.51]Just then, a man hurried to the ticket office. | 正在这时，一位男子匆匆奔向售票处。
[00:46.59]'Can I return these two tickets?' he asked. | “我可以退掉这两张票吗？”他问。
[00:51.15]'Certainly,' the girl said. | “当然可以，”那姑娘说。
[00:55.05]I went back to the ticket office at once. | 我马上又回到售票处。
[00:59.44]'Could I have those two tickets please?' I asked. | “我可以买那两张票吗？”我问。
[01:05.21]'Certainly,' the girl said, | “当然可以，”姑娘说，
[01:08.69]'but they're for next Wednesday's performance. | “不过这两张票是下星期三演出的。
[01:12.40]Do you still want them?' | 您还要吗？”
[01:15.35]'I might as well have them,' I said sadly. | “我还是买下的好，”我沮丧地说。
